{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:0d224534f197a9d3","name":"Holding Cells","source":{"id":"source:reference-0d224534f197a9d3","title":"Holding Cells","revision":19682,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T22:24:47Z","sha256":"26e5ba3e0ca4b999aaef78a6b2bda933ca75d66462a9921af8bd4570df3bc795","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19682","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Holding%20Cells&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-0d224534f197a9d3","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}," "]},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["HOLDING CELLS\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["EP\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["AVAILABILITY\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["COST\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["25% of Passengers\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["1,000 (Base)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["50% of Passengers\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["2,000 (Base)\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["75% of Passengers\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["4\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Military"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Military"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["5,000 (Base)\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Holding Cells (often referred to as the brig or the detection block) are standard on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"}," and some smaller vessels (including patrol ships). Bounty hunters and pirates find it useful to add them to other vessels, and private \"dungeon ships\" convert the majority of their space to Holding Cells to act as for-hire prison transports. Up to 75% of a Starship's Passengers can be converted to Holding Cells.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["A Holding Cell has reinforced walls (DR 10, 150 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},"), an advanced lock (DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check to bypass from the outside, DC 30 to bypass from the inside), and cameras and sensors that allow it to be monitored from remote stations (+5 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Equipment"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Equipment","referenceId":"reference:7f2465ac7cefab27"}," bonus on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," checks made into the cell from the security post). A small port allows food and similar small items to be passed safely into the cell without exposing the jailer, and it can be used to make ranged weapon attacks into the cell (such as when it's necessary to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"}," a troublesome prisoner). Cells also include an armored ring (DR 10, 50 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},") to which ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binder Cuffs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binder_Cuffs","referenceId":"reference:39a1390ff55032c9"}," and similar restraints can be attached.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
